Development Request — Editable Strategic Focus During Realignment
Prepared for:  Software development team
Prepared by:  OneVoice27 / HCI product team
Date:  August 25, 2026
Applies to:  Proposal edit mode while a proposal is in the Realignment stage
Version:  1.0 — Draft for estimation
 
1.  Background & the defect
When a proposal is sent back for realignment, the submitter opens it in edit mode to make the requested changes. Comparing the read (view) layout with the edit layout reveals a gap: the Strategic Focus block appears in the read view but is missing from the edit view, so those fields cannot currently be changed during realignment.
The affected fields (present in the read view, absent in edit mode) are:
●      Strategic Focus (e.g., “Prayer, Training, and Inspiration”)
●      What strategic objective is this? (e.g., “1.5 – Cultivate Mission Learning and Innovation”)
●      What strategic activity is this? (the strategic-activity description)
●      Accountable (the accountable person, e.g., name and email)
This request makes the Strategic Focus block editable in edit mode during realignment, restricted to users in GC departments and institutions.
  E1  Editable Strategic Focus during realignment 
Expose the Strategic Focus block in proposal edit mode when a proposal is in realignment, and let authorized GC users edit it, so requested realignment changes to strategy can actually be made.
E1-S1  Show and edit Strategic Focus fields in edit mode
As a GC department / institution user editing a proposal sent back for realignment,
I want the Strategic Focus fields to appear and be editable in edit mode,
so that I can make the strategy changes requested during realignment.
Acceptance criteria
●      In edit mode, the Strategic Focus block is shown with the same fields that appear in the read view: Strategic Focus, What strategic objective is this?, What strategic activity is this?, and Accountable.
●      Each field is populated with its current saved value and is editable using the appropriate input (dropdown vs. free text vs. person picker) consistent with how it was originally captured.
●      Edits save with the rest of the proposal and persist on resubmission.
●      The read view and edit view now show the same set of Strategic Focus fields — no field that is visible when reading is missing when editing.
●      Each change to a Strategic Focus field is recorded in the change log (field, from → to, user, timestamp).
Note: This closes the discrepancy between the read layout (which shows Strategic Focus) and the edit layout (which currently omits it).
E1-S2  Restrict editing to GC departments and institutions
As an organization,
I want only users in GC departments and institutions to edit the Strategic Focus,
so that strategic alignment stays under the control of the appropriate GC entities.
Acceptance criteria
●      Users who belong to a GC department / institution can edit the Strategic Focus fields during realignment.
●      Users who do not belong to a GC department / institution do not get editable Strategic Focus fields — they continue to see those fields as read-only.
●      The permission is enforced server-side, not just hidden in the UI, so a non-GC user cannot save changes to these fields via direct request.
●      Behavior is unchanged for all other proposal fields and for stages other than realignment.
 
End of request — OneVoice27 Proposal Portal, editable Strategic Focus during realignment.
  



  

