Development Request — Move a Proposal Between Departments
Prepared for:  Software development team
Prepared by:  OneVoice27 / HCI product team
Date:  September 22, 2026
Applies to:  Global admin and Technical secretary — budget management across departments
Related:  Reserve department move (same budget-transaction pattern)
Version:  1.0 — Draft for estimation
 
1.  Background & purpose
Each department has its own budget total, and proposals draw down against the budget of the department they belong to. A global admin or technical secretary needs to be able to move a proposal from one department to another — regardless of the proposal’s status, including approved proposals — and have the budgets on both sides re-balanced automatically.
When a proposal is moved, two budget effects must occur together: the destination department’s available funds are reduced by the proposal’s amount (it now carries the cost), and the originating department’s available funds are increased by the proposal’s amount (it is released from the cost). In effect, the cost follows the proposal to its new department.
2.  Definitions
●      Originating department — the department the proposal currently belongs to and whose budget it currently draws from.
●      Destination department — the department the proposal is being moved to, which will carry its cost after the move.
●      Authorized mover — a user with the Global admin or Technical secretary role, permitted to perform this move.
  E1  Move a proposal between departments 
A global admin or technical secretary can move a proposal of any status from one department to another, with the destination budget reduced and the originating budget increased accordingly.
E1-S1  Move a proposal of any status and re-balance budgets
As a global admin or technical secretary,
I want to move a proposal from one department to another regardless of its status,
so that the proposal sits in the correct department and its cost moves with it.
Acceptance criteria
●      An authorized mover (Global admin or Technical secretary) can move a proposal from its current department to any other department.
●      A proposal can be moved regardless of status — including approved proposals, and proposals in draft, review, realignment, or any other state.
●      On the move, the destination department’s available funds are reduced (decreased) by the proposal’s amount.
●      On the move, the originating department’s available funds are increased by the proposal’s amount.
●      Both budget effects happen together as a single transaction; neither occurs without the other.
●      The proposal is thereafter associated with the destination department.
●      Only the Global admin and Technical secretary roles can perform this move; the capability is enforced server-side.
Open question: Confirm the exact amount used for the re-balance — the proposal’s approved/allocated amount, or its remaining/uncharged balance if spending has already begun.
E1-S2  Preserve the proposal’s status on move
As an authorized mover,
I want the proposal to keep its status when it moves to the destination department,
so that the move relocates the proposal without disrupting its place in the workflow.
Acceptance criteria
●      The proposal’s status is unchanged by the move — an approved proposal stays approved; an in-review proposal stays in review; and so on.
●      The move changes only the owning department and re-balances the budgets (per E1-S1); it does not reset or advance the workflow status.
●      The project code (which reflects the department/account) should be updated to the destination department’s account code on move, consistent with the Reserve department behavior.
E1-S3  Confirm the move and record it for audit
As an authorized mover,
I want to confirm the move and have it recorded,
so that the budget change is intentional and fully traceable.
Acceptance criteria
●      Before the move completes, the mover sees a confirmation showing the proposal, the originating department, the destination department, and the amount that will move.
●      After the move, the originating department, the destination department, and the proposal all reflect the updated balances immediately.
●      The move is recorded in the audit trail: the proposal, from-department → to-department, the amount, the user who performed it (and their role), and the timestamp.
●      If the destination department does not have sufficient available funds, the behavior is defined (block with a clear message, or allow with a warning — confirm).
●      The change flows through to financial reporting (e.g., the GC Financials Workbook) so downstream figures stay consistent.
 
End of request — OneVoice27 Proposal Portal, move a proposal between departments.


