Development Request — Editable & Tracked Division Budget Allocations
Prepared for:  Software development team
Prepared by:  OneVoice27 / HCI product team
Date:  September 22, 2026
Applies to:  Global admin — division / department budget allocation
Related:  Reserve department move; Move a proposal between departments; Initiative tags
Version:  1.0 — Draft for estimation
 
1.  Background & purpose
Divisions are beginning to give up part of their overall budget so it can be reallocated elsewhere. For example, SPD (South Pacific Division) — and potentially other divisions — may release budget that is then reassigned to other departments/divisions.
The global admin needs to be able to edit the approved budget allocation for a division, lock it in, and have every change tracked. When an amount is removed from one division and reallocated to another, both sides of the move must be recorded with a note explaining where the money is moving to and from, so there is a complete, auditable history of allocation changes.
2.  Definitions
●      Division / department allocation — the approved budget amount assigned to a division or department.
●      Reallocation — moving an amount out of one division’s allocation and into another’s.
●      Locked allocation — an approved allocation the global admin has finalized so it cannot be edited until deliberately unlocked/adjusted.
●      Allocation history — the tracked record of every allocation edit and reallocation, including amounts, from/to, note, who, and when.
3.  Scope at a glance
Three epics are in scope. Full stories follow in section 5.
 
Epic
	Feature
	Primary actor
	E1
	Edit and lock a division’s approved budget allocation
	Global admin
	E2
	Reallocate an amount between divisions with a required note
	Global admin
	E3
	Allocation history / audit trail
	Global admin / Treasury
	4.  Cross-cutting requirements
●      All allocation edits and reallocations are permission-restricted to the global admin and enforced server-side.
●      Budget math must stay balanced: an amount removed from one division must be accounted for (reallocated or explicitly held), never lost.
●      Changes flow through to dependent figures (department available funds, financial reporting / GC Financials Workbook).
●      Every change is timestamped and attributed to the user who made it.
5.  Epics & stories
  E1  Edit and lock a division’s approved budget 
The global admin can adjust a division’s approved allocation and lock it once finalized.
E1-S1  Edit a division’s approved budget allocation
As a global admin,
I want to edit the approved budget allocation for a division,
so that I can reflect a division giving up or receiving budget.
Acceptance criteria
●      The global admin can change a division’s approved allocation amount (increase or decrease).
●      The edit updates the division’s allocation and its available funds accordingly.
●      Only the global admin can edit an allocation; enforced server-side.
●      Every edit is written to the allocation history (Epic E3).
E1-S2  Lock an approved allocation
As a global admin,
I want to lock a division’s approved allocation once it is finalized,
so that the approved amount is protected from further change until deliberately adjusted.
Acceptance criteria
●      The global admin can lock a division’s approved allocation.
●      While locked, the allocation cannot be edited by anyone until it is unlocked/adjusted by the global admin.
●      Locking and unlocking are recorded in the allocation history (who and when).
●      A reallocation (Epic E2) cannot act on a locked allocation directly, it must be unlocked first.
  E2  Reallocate an amount between divisions 
When budget is removed from one division and given to another, the move is recorded as a single reallocation with a required note.
E2-S1  Move an amount from one division to another
As a global admin,
I want to remove an amount from one division and reallocate it to another,
so that released budget (e.g., from SPD) is reassigned where it is needed.
Acceptance criteria
●      The global admin can specify a source division, a destination, and an amount to reallocate.
●      The amount is deducted from the source division’s allocation and added to the destination’s allocation.
●      Both sides happen together as a single transaction; the total across divisions is conserved.
●      A division’s allocation cannot be reduced below what it has already committed/spent (behavior confirmed with product).
●      The destination is always another division/department, (not yet assigned) is NOT allowed.
E2-S2  Require a note for every reallocation
As a global admin,
I want to record a note for where the money is moving to and from,
so that the reason and direction of each reallocation are clear in the history.
Acceptance criteria
●      Each reallocation requires a note describing the movement (from where, to where, and why).
●      The from-division, to-division, amount, and note are captured together on the reallocation record.
●      The reallocation cannot be completed without the note.
  E3  Allocation history / audit trail 
Every allocation edit, lock, and reallocation is tracked so the full history of division budgets is auditable.
E3-S1  Track a full history of allocation changes
As a global admin or Treasury reviewer,
I want a tracked history of every allocation change,
so that I can see how each division’s budget reached its current amount.
Acceptance criteria
●      Every allocation edit, lock/unlock, and reallocation is recorded with: the amount, previous → new value (for edits), from-division → to-division (for reallocations), the note, the user, and the timestamp.
●      The history is viewable per division and across the reallocation of amounts between divisions.
●      History entries are immutable — they cannot be edited or deleted.
●      The history reconciles: the sum of a division’s recorded changes equals its current allocation.
E3-S2  View reallocations from both sides
As a global admin or Treasury reviewer,
I want each reallocation to be visible from both the giving and receiving division,
so that the movement of money is clear from either end.
Acceptance criteria
●      A reallocation appears in the source division’s history as an outbound movement and in the destination’s as an inbound movement.
●      Both views show the amount, the counterpart division, the note, the user, and the timestamp.
●      The history is exportable / available to financial reporting.
 
End of request — OneVoice27 Proposal Portal, editable & tracked division budget allocations.


