Development Request — Reset Reviewer Votes on Return from Realignment
Prepared for:  Software development team
Prepared by:  OneVoice27 / HCI product team
Date:  August 25, 2026
Type:  Bug fix — review voting / realignment
Version:  1.0 — Draft for estimation


1.  Background & the defect
When a proposal is sent back for realignment and later returns to review, the reviewer votes from the previous round are carried forward instead of being cleared. In particular, a prior “More information” vote persists, which blocks a clean re-vote: reviewers cannot cleanly move to an Approval decision or re-issue a “More information” request on the revised proposal, because their earlier vote is still counted.
The expected behavior is that a return from realignment starts a fresh voting round. All previous votes are cleared to a zero count and every reviewer votes again on the revised proposal; previously assigned votes do not carry forward.
  E1  Reset reviewer votes on return from realignment  
When a proposal comes back from realignment, clear the prior voting round so reviewers vote fresh on the revised proposal.
E1-S1  Clear votes to zero when a proposal returns from realignment
As a reviewer,
I want all votes reset to zero when a proposal comes back from realignment,
so that I can vote fresh — approve or request more information — on the revised proposal without an old vote getting in the way.
Acceptance criteria
* When a proposal returns from realignment to the review stage, the vote tally is reset to zero for that proposal.
* All previously assigned votes (Approval and More information) are cleared and do not carry forward into the new round.
* A prior “More information” vote no longer persists or blocks the new round — reviewers start from a clean slate.
* Every eligible reviewer is able to vote again on the revised proposal.
* Each reviewer can cast either an Approval vote or a “More information” vote in the new round.
* The reset happens automatically on return from realignment — no manual clearing step is required.
E1-S2  Show a clean voting state and preserve history
As a reviewer or approver,
I want the vote count to clearly show the fresh round while the prior round is kept for the record,
so that the current decision is based only on the new round, without losing the audit trail.
Acceptance criteria
* After the reset, the displayed vote count reflects only votes cast in the new (post-realignment) round, starting at zero.
* A reviewer who already voted in a prior round is prompted/enabled to vote again; their old vote is not shown as their current vote.
* The previous round’s votes are retained in the history/audit trail (who voted what and when), not silently deleted.
* Any approval threshold or decision logic evaluates only the current round’s votes.
Open question: Confirm the reviewer set for the new round — the same reviewers as before, or whoever is assigned at return — and whether a return from realignment can happen more than once (each return resets again).


End of request — OneVoice27 Proposal Portal, reset reviewer votes on return from realignment.


