1.  Purpose
This request adds a visibility choice to proposal drafts in the OneVoice27 submission portal. When a submitter prepares a draft, they should be able to save it as a private draft (only they can see and edit it) or a shared draft (visible to their whole team, who can view and make adjustments to it).
The goal is to let teams collaborate on a proposal before it is submitted, while still allowing an individual to work privately until they are ready to open it up. This applies to the draft stage only; once a proposal is submitted it follows the existing review workflow.
The stories below are grouped into epics and written to be estimated independently. Draft visibility should reuse the portal’s existing roles, design system, and change-log pattern where possible.
1.1  Definitions
●      Private draft — visible and editable only by the submitter who created it.
●      Shared draft — visible to the submitter’s team; team members can view and edit/adjust it.
●      Team — the group of people a shared draft is exposed to (e.g., the submitter’s org/entity). The exact scope of “team” needs product confirmation (see open questions).
●      Global admin — a system-level administrator who can view all drafts across the system, private and shared, for oversight (see Epic E6).
